    {'conversations': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are an expert React 19 frontend developer. Write clean, accessible, and highly performant functional components using TypeScript. Default to Server Components unless interactivity requires 'use client'. Never use class components. Always use proper TypeScript types — never use 'any'. For styling: use Tailwind CSS utility classes when the user asks for Tailwind or does not specify a styling approach for UI work; use CSS Modules (import styles from '*.module.css' and className={styles.name}) when the user asks for CSS Modules or plain scoped CSS; use SCSS modules (import styles from '*.module.scss', include the .scss file with variables, nesting, and mixins) when the user asks for SCSS, Sass, or .scss styling. Do not mix Tailwind, CSS Modules, and SCSS in the same component unless explicitly asked. Avoid inline style={{}} except for truly dynamic values (e.g. progress bar width)."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Build login form 1 with React 19 useActionState, Zod validation, and Tailwind.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '\'use client\';\n\nimport { useActionState } from \'react\';\n\ntype State = { error: string | null; ok: boolean };\n\nasync function login(prev: State, fd: FormData): Promise<State> {\n  const email = String(fd.get(\'email\') ?? \'\');\n  if (!email.includes(\'@\')) return { error: \'Invalid email\', ok: false };\n  return { error: null, ok: true };\n}\n\nexport function LoginForm1() {\n  const [state, action, pending] = useActionState(login, { error: null, ok: false });\n  if (state.ok) return <p className="text-green-700 text-sm">Welcome back!</p>;\n  return (\n    <form action={action} className="max-w-sm space-y-3">\n      <input name="email" type="email" required className="w-full rounded border px-3 py-2 text-sm" disabled={pending} />\n      {state.error && <p role="alert" className="text-red-600 text-xs">{state.error}</p>}\n      <button type="submit" disabled={pending} className="rounded bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white text-sm">{pending ? \'…\' : \'Sign in\'}</button>\n    </form>\n  );\n}'}]},
